\description{
\code{ds_theme()} sets the look of a \code{\link[=dynaspec]{dynaspec()}} object (axes, text, panels, colors and player controls), in the same way for all styles. Adding it again changes the settings supplied (other settings are kept). Preset themes (e.g. \code{ds_theme_dark()}) set several settings at once.
}
\details{
Only the settings supplied are used; other settings take the defaults of each style. Settings supplied in other layers (e.g. the palette in \code{\link[=ds_spectrogram]{ds_spectrogram()}}) take precedence over those of the theme.

Preset themes are complete themes: adding one replaces previous themes (use \code{ds_theme()} afterwards to change some of its settings, or supply them in the preset):
\itemize{
\item \code{ds_theme_dark()}: black background, white text, 'mako' palette.
\item \code{ds_theme_mako()}: light theme with the 'mako' palette (reversed: light background and dark sounds) and 'mako' colors for panels, annotations, play line and player controls.
\item \code{ds_theme_presentation()}: large bold text for slides and projectors.
\item \code{ds_theme_paper()}: black and white with serif fonts, for printed figures.
\item \code{ds_theme_minimal()}: no boxes, light gray axes and short ticks.
\item \code{ds_theme_transparent()}: transparent background, to blend in slides or web pages of any color.
\item \code{ds_theme_void()}: no axes, titles or boxes (only the sound).
\item \code{ds_theme_macaulay()}: inspired by the player of the 'Macaulay Library': gray spectrogram, compact axes (time in minutes and seconds above the figure) and a black player bar with a square play button. Best with \code{\link[=ds_scrolling]{ds_scrolling()}} and an \code{\link[=ds_overview]{ds_overview()}} (e.g. \code{ds_scrolling(t.display = 1.5, fix.time = FALSE)}).
\item \code{ds_theme_xenocanto()}: inspired by the player of the 'Xeno-canto' web site: gray spectrogram, labels inside the figure, solid play line and rounded player controls with a seek bar. Best with \code{\link[=ds_scrolling]{ds_scrolling()}} and an \code{\link[=ds_oscillogram]{ds_oscillogram()}} (e.g. \code{ds_scrolling(t.display = 1.5, fix.time = FALSE)}).
}
